The SDL2 fallback ("Standard Gamepad") binds the right stick Y the wrong
way round: up reads as down. SDL gamepad axes are negative upwards, as
the left stick binds in the same block already assume (+1 plus, -1
minus). The XInput-style blocks elsewhere use up-positive axes and are
left alone.

--- a/input/input_autodetect_builtin.c
+++ b/input/input_autodetect_builtin.c
@@ -63,8 +63,8 @@
 DECL_AXIS(l_y_minus, -1) \
 DECL_AXIS(r_x_plus,  +2) \
 DECL_AXIS(r_x_minus, -2) \
-DECL_AXIS(r_y_plus,  -3) \
-DECL_AXIS(r_y_minus, +3)
+DECL_AXIS(r_y_plus,  +3) \
+DECL_AXIS(r_y_minus, -3)
 
 #if defined(DINGUX) && defined(HAVE_SDL_DINGUX)
 #define DINGUX_SDL_DEFAULT_BINDS \
